{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-74741","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106070","text":"Skill 01 — The Ten Protocols"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74743","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106071","text":"OS-001 through OS-010: what each protocol specifies, which product implements it, and the cognitive science behind it. Eight cognitive primitives plus two cross-cutting protocols (PRISM diagnostic, PULSE temporal)."}]}],"id":"blk-74742","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-74744","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106072","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-74745","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106073","text":"OpenSentience publishes ten numbered protocols organized in two layers:"}]},{"id":"blk-74746","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74748","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106074","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive primitives (OS-001 — OS-008)"},{"id":"spn-106075","text":" — eight individual capabilities,"}]}],"id":"blk-74747","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74749","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106076","text":"each grounded in a cognitive science thread."}]},{"id":"blk-74750","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106077","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cross-cutting protocols (OS-009 PRISM, OS-010 PULSE)"},{"id":"spn-106078","text":" — two sibling"}]}],"id":"blk-74751","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74753","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106079","text":"protocols that sit above the cognitive primitives and above the [&] structural composition layer. PULSE declares how every loop in the ecosystem cycles, nests, and signals; PRISM measures how well those loops actually learn over time."}]},{"id":"blk-74754","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106080","text":"The protocols are independent specifications — they can be adopted individually or composed together. A system may publish a PULSE manifest without implementing any cognitive primitive, and PRISM can benchmark any PULSE-conforming system without bespoke per-system integration."}]},{"id":"blk-74755","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106081","text":"OS-001: Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-74756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106082","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106083","text":" Hippocampal consolidation (McClelland et al. 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-74757","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106084","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74758","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106085","text":"Three node types: episodic (events), semantic (facts), procedural (workflows)"}]}],"id":"blk-74759","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74762","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106086","text":"Typed, weighted edges between nodes"}]}],"id":"blk-74761","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74764","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106087","text":"Confidence scores with evidence-calibrated assignment"}]}],"id":"blk-74763","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74766","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106088","text":"Consolidation cycle: decay low-confidence nodes, prune stale entries,"}]}],"id":"blk-74765","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106089","text":"merge near-duplicates, strengthen co-retrieved edges"}]},{"id":"blk-74768","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74770","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106090","text":"Memory timescales: working memory (session), short-term (hours), long-term"}]}],"id":"blk-74769","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106091","text":"(persistent)"}]},{"id":"blk-74772","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106092","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106093","text":" New memories must be stored quickly (hippocampal fast-write) without disrupting existing knowledge (neocortical slow-consolidation). This maps to immediate ETS/SQLite writes with background consolidation."}]},{"id":"blk-74773","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106094","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106095","text":" Graphonomous ("},{"id":"spn-106096","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-106097","text":", "},{"id":"spn-106098","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-106099","text":", "},{"id":"spn-106100","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-106101","text":", "},{"id":"spn-106102","marks":["code"],"text":"run_consolidation"},{"id":"spn-106103","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-74774","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106104","text":"OS-002: Topological Routing (kappa)"}]},{"id":"blk-74775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106105","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106106","text":" Working memory gating (O'Reilly & Frank 2006)"}]},{"id":"blk-74776","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106107","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74777","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106108","text":"The kappa parameter: a measure of cyclicity in a knowledge subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-74778","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106109","text":"Strongly connected component (SCC) detection on retrieved neighborhoods"}]}],"id":"blk-74780","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106110","text":"Routing decision: kappa = 0 implies fast path (acyclic, no conflict),"}]}],"id":"blk-74782","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74784","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106111","text":"kappa > 0 implies deliberate path (cycles exist, may contain contradictions)"}]},{"id":"blk-74785","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106112","text":"Topological features: SCC count, max SCC size, edge density within cycles"}]}],"id":"blk-74786","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74788","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106113","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106114","text":" The prefrontal cortex gates information into working memory based on relevance and conflict signals. Kappa serves as the conflict signal — cyclic knowledge regions indicate unresolved tension that requires deliberation before action."}]},{"id":"blk-74789","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106115","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106116","text":" Graphonomous routing layer ("},{"id":"spn-106117","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"},{"id":"spn-106118","text":", "},{"id":"spn-106119","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-106120","text":" topology annotations)"}]},{"id":"blk-74790","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106121","text":"OS-003: Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-74791","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106122","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106123","text":" Dual-process theory (Kahneman 2011)"}]},{"id":"blk-74792","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106124","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74793","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74795","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106125","text":"Four-phase deliberation: bid, debate, vote, commit"}]}],"id":"blk-74794","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74797","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106126","text":"Argumentation framework: claims, warrants, rebuttals"}]}],"id":"blk-74796","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74799","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106127","text":"Consensus mechanisms: majority, supermajority, unanimity"}]}],"id":"blk-74798","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74801","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106128","text":"Timeout and escalation policies"}]}],"id":"blk-74800","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74803","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106129","text":"Triggered when kappa routing indicates deliberation is needed"}]}],"id":"blk-74802","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106130","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106131","text":" System 1 (fast, automatic) handles routine decisions. System 2 (slow, deliberate) engages when conflict is detected. The kappa threshold is the trigger that shifts from fast to deliberate processing."}]},{"id":"blk-74805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106132","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106133","text":" AgenTroMatic ("},{"id":"spn-106134","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-106135","text":" tool in Graphonomous provides the single-agent deliberation path)"}]},{"id":"blk-74806","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106136","text":"OS-004: Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-74807","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106137","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106138","text":" Endogenous attention (Desimone & Duncan 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-74808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106139","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74809","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74811","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106140","text":"Three-phase cycle: survey (scan environment), triage (rank by salience),"}]}],"id":"blk-74810","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106141","text":"dispatch (act on highest-priority items)"}]},{"id":"blk-74813","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74815","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106142","text":"Salience scoring: combines urgency, recency, goal relevance, and confidence"}]}],"id":"blk-74814","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74817","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106143","text":"Goal bias: active goals increase salience of related knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-74816","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74819","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106144","text":"Dispatch modes: act (execute), learn (gather more context), escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74818","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106145","text":"(request human intervention), idle (nothing needed)"}]},{"id":"blk-74821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106146","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106147","text":" Biological attention is goal-directed (endogenous) not just stimulus-driven (exogenous). The attention engine prioritizes based on the agent's active goals, not just what is new or loud."}]},{"id":"blk-74822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106148","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106149","text":" Graphonomous attention module ("},{"id":"spn-106150","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-106151","text":", "},{"id":"spn-106152","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"},{"id":"spn-106153","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-74823","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106154","text":"OS-005: Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-74824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106155","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106156","text":" Resource rationality (Lieder & Griffiths 2020)"}]},{"id":"blk-74825","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106157","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74826","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74828","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106158","text":"Three tiers: "},{"id":"spn-106159","marks":["code"],"text":"local_small"},{"id":"spn-106160","text":" (8B parameter models), "},{"id":"spn-106161","marks":["code"],"text":"local_large"},{"id":"spn-106162","text":" (70B+),"}]}],"id":"blk-74827","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106163","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud_frontier"},{"id":"spn-106164","text":" (largest available)"}]},{"id":"blk-74830","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106165","text":"Same topology and tool surface at every tier — only depth and latency differ"}]}],"id":"blk-74831","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106166","text":"Escalation rules: when local_small confidence is below threshold, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74833","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74835","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106167","text":"to local_large; when local_large is insufficient, escalate to cloud_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-74836","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106168","text":"Budget constraints: token limits, latency targets, cost caps per tier"}]}],"id":"blk-74837","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106169","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106170","text":" Optimal cognition allocates computational resources proportional to decision importance. Simple decisions use fast/cheap processing; high-stakes decisions justify expensive computation."}]},{"id":"blk-74840","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106171","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106172","text":" Graphonomous and Agentelic (tier selection and escalation logic)"}]},{"id":"blk-74841","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106173","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-74842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106174","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106175","text":" Executive function (Miyake et al. 2000)"}]},{"id":"blk-74843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106176","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74844","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74846","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106177","text":"Permission taxonomy: filesystem, network, tool_invocation, graph_access"}]}],"id":"blk-74845","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106178","text":"Lifecycle state machine: installed, enabled, running, disabled, removed"}]}],"id":"blk-74847","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74850","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106179","text":"Graduated autonomy: observe, advise, act"}]}],"id":"blk-74849","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74852","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106180","text":"Append-only audit trail with typed events"}]}],"id":"blk-74851","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106181","text":"OTP-native implementation: GenStateMachine, ETS, DynamicSupervisor"}]}],"id":"blk-74853","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106182","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-106183","text":" Executive function provides inhibitory control (permissions), task switching (lifecycle), and cognitive flexibility (autonomy levels). Without executive function, an agent cannot self-regulate — it either does nothing or does everything."}]},{"id":"blk-74856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106184","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106185","text":" "},{"id":"spn-106186","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-106187","text":" hex package (this project)"}]},{"id":"blk-74857","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106188","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-74858","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106189","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106190","text":" Immune system — self/non-self discrimination"}]},{"id":"blk-74859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106191","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74860","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106192","text":"Five threat categories: prompt injection, model poisoning, side-channel,"}]}],"id":"blk-74861","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106193","text":"identity spoofing, resource exhaustion"}]},{"id":"blk-74864","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106194","text":"Detection rules per category"}]}],"id":"blk-74865","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74868","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106195","text":"Defense protocols: quarantine, circuit-break, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74867","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74870","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106196","text":"Integration with OS-006 for permission revocation and OS-008 for circuit"}]}],"id":"blk-74869","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106197","text":"breaking"}]},{"id":"blk-74872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106198","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106199","text":" OpenSentience security module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-74873","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106200","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-74874","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106201","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106202","text":" Supervisory attentional system (Norman & Shallice 1986)"}]},{"id":"blk-74875","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106203","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74876","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74878","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106204","text":"Pipeline ordering enforcement (retrieve → route → act → learn)"}]}],"id":"blk-74877","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74880","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106205","text":"Quality gates between pipeline stages"}]}],"id":"blk-74879","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74882","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106206","text":"Sprint contracts: bounded execution with explicit goals and success criteria"}]}],"id":"blk-74881","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106207","text":"Context management: 60% threshold, compaction, Graphonomous overflow"}]}],"id":"blk-74883","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74886","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106208","text":"Generator-evaluator separation for adversarial grading"}]}],"id":"blk-74885","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106209","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106210","text":" OpenSentience harness module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-74888","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106211","text":"OS-009: PRISM — Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory"}]},{"id":"blk-74889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106212","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106213","text":" Meta-cognition + psychometrics (Item Response Theory, signal detection theory)"}]},{"id":"blk-74890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106214","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74891","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106215","text":"9 continual-learning dimensions (retention, plasticity, transfer,"}]}],"id":"blk-74892","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106216","text":"contradiction handling, etc.)"}]},{"id":"blk-74895","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106217","text":"4-phase evaluation loop: compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose"}]}],"id